20:T465,Applies to ontologies (OWL/OBO/RDF artefacts). Logical consistency carries half the weight: a reasoner run (ROBOT + ELK, run by NeuroSchema on every ontology; the OBO Dashboard's result is used only if ours is missing) that finds the ontology consistent with no unsatisfiable classes scores 10; consistent with 1–5 unsatisfiable classes 5; more than 5 → 2; inconsistent, or the file could not be loaded, 0. OWL 2 DL profile 2. Upper-ontology alignment: imports or uses terms from BFO, COB, DOLCE, GFO or gUFO 3, the Relation Ontology 1 (read from the file as well as OLS and Bioregistry). Quality report: no ROBOT errors 2, warnings per class ≤ 0.05 → 1 (both only for OBO-style ontologies, since the ROBOT report checks OBO conventions), and a pitfall scan with no critical pitfalls 1. A check that could not be run (no retrievable artefact, file too large, tool timed out) is not assessed: its points are left out of the possible total, and the grade is flagged "Q partially assessed". Schemas, atlases and other non-ontology resources are not scored on Q; their total is scaled to 100 from the remaining 80 points.1a:["$","tr","quality",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","b",null,{"className":"sym","children":"Q"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Ontology consistency & quality",null,["$","p",null,{"className":"small muted","children":"$20"}]]}],["$","td",null,{"className":"num","children":20}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"c(logical consistency) + 2·[OWL 2 DL] + u(upper ontology) + q(quality report)"}]}]]}]
1b:["$","tr","maintenance",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","b",null,{"className":"sym","children":"M"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Maintenance",null,["$","p",null,{"className":"small muted","children":"Recency of the latest commit, release or dated file: ≤ 3 months 10, ≤ 6 months 8, ≤ 1 year 5, ≤ 2 years 2, older 0. Release cadence — distinct releases in the last 12 months (GitHub releases, dated tags, version IRIs across runs): ≥ 6 → 6, ≥ 4 → 5, ≥ 2 → 3, 1 → 2."}]]}],["$","td",null,{"className":"num","children":16}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"recency(months) + cadence(releases in last 12 months)"}]}]]}]
1c:["$","tr","adoption",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","b",null,{"className":"sym","children":"U"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Community adoption",null,["$","p",null,{"className":"small muted","children":"Documented adopting projects (curated, OBO Foundry usages): ≥ 8 → 7, ≥ 5 → 5, ≥ 3 → 4, ≥ 1 → 2. Reuse — other ontologies that import it (OBO Dashboard, OLS, Bioregistry): ≥ 30 → 4, ≥ 10 → 3, ≥ 3 → 2, ≥ 1 → 1. Community signal, the better of GitHub stars (≥ 500 → 5, ≥ 100 → 4, ≥ 25 → 2, ≥ 5 → 1) and reference-paper citations (≥ 1000 → 5, ≥ 300 → 4, ≥ 50 → 2, ≥ 10 → 1)."}]]}],["$","td",null,{"className":"num","children":16}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"a(adopting projects) + reuse(ontologies importing it) + max(stars, citations)"}]}]]}]
1d:["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":["$","b",null,{"className":"sym","children":"P"}]}],["$","td",null,{"children":["Penalties (inactivity & inconsistency)",["$","p",null,{"className":"small muted","children":"Problems are marked down, not just left unrewarded. Inactivity: after a one-year grace period every further year without public activity deducts 4 points (up to 20); archived, legacy or OBO-inactive resources lose a further 10; with no activity evidence at all, 5. Consistency: a logically inconsistent ontology loses 20 and can score no higher than 54 (grade D). Critical pitfalls (OOPS!, e.g. cycles in the class hierarchy, multiple domains/ranges, ambiguous namespace) cost 3 per pitfall type, up to 12. Unsatisfiable classes and ROBOT report errors already cost Q points, so they are not penalised again here. The penalty is capped at 50 and the total never drops below 0."}]]}],["$","td",null,{"className":"num","children":"—"}],["$","td",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"min(50, inactivity + 10·[archived/legacy/OBO-inactive] + 20·[inconsistent] + min(12, 3·critical pitfall types)). Inconsistent ontologies are capped at 54 (grade D)."}]}]]}]
